.Dd September 23, 2026
.Dt PAZARI-AGENT 1
.Os pazari
.Sh NAME
.Nm pazari-agent
.Nd guest memory agent for pazari
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl c Ar path
.Nm
.Op Fl c Ar path
.Cm panic-open
.Nm
.Op Fl c Ar path
.Cm preflight
.Nm
.Op Fl c Ar path
.Cm example-config
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
runs inside a virtual machine and negotiates that machine's memory with
.Xr pazarid 1
on the host.
It watches one cgroup, brakes the workload in it with
.Va memory.high
rather than letting the kernel kill it, asks the host for more memory when the
brake starts to bite, and offers memory back when the workload stops wanting
it.
.Pp
The agent writes
.Va memory.high
and
.Va memory.max
on that cgroup, and nothing else in the guest should.
It does not start, stop or restart the workload, and it does not decide what
the workload may do.
.Pp
With no subcommand the agent runs in the foreground until it is asked to stop.
It reads its configuration once, at startup; there is no reload.
.Ss What it does
The agent holds one of five modes, published as
.Va pazari_agent_mode :
.Bl -tag -width "awaiting_grant" -offset indent
.It Cm titrating
Finding the workload's working set, once, at startup, by lowering
.Va memory.high
from
.Va memory.max
a step at a time for as long as the workload is quiet.
.It Cm steady
The workload is progressing.
.Va memory.high
sits a whole burst reserve below
.Va memory.max .
.It Cm awaiting_grant
The kernel is throttling the workload and the agent has asked the host for more
memory.
The band is open: the workload may burst to within
.Cm open_guard
of
.Va memory.max
while the request is in flight.
.It Cm releasing
The workload has been idle for long enough that the agent is reclaiming memory
out of its cgroup so as to offer it back to the host.
.It Cm exhausted
The workload wants more than the host will give it.
What happens next is
.Cm engine.exhaustion :
either the band stays open and the workload degrades, or it collapses onto
.Va memory.max
and the workload is killed as a unit.
.El
.Pp
The arithmetic behind those bands, and how to size the three reserves that
place them, is in
.Xr pazari-agent.toml 5 .
.Ss Shutdown
On
.Dv SIGTERM
or
.Dv SIGINT
the agent takes the brake off before it exits: it writes
.Va memory.high
back to
.Cm max ,
so the workload is left unthrottled rather than pinned at whatever limit the
agent happened to have set.
.Pp
It cannot do that if it is killed outright, which is what
.Cm panic-open
is for.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl c Ar path , Fl -config Ar path
The configuration file.
The default is
.Pa /etc/pazari/agent.toml .
Accepted before or after a subcommand.
.It Fl -version
Print the version and exit.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.El
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm panic-open
Take the brake off the workload cgroup and exit.
.Pp
This writes
.Va memory.high
back to
.Cm max
and does nothing else.
It is meant for
.Va ExecStopPost ,
where it runs after every exit the agent makes, orderly or not.
Without it, an agent that is killed leaves the workload braked at limits
nothing will ever move again, and the workload stalls until something notices.
.Pp
It is safe to run when no agent is running and safe to run twice.
.It Cm preflight
Run the checks the agent runs at startup, print what they found, and exit.
.Pp
See
.Sx PREFLIGHT .
.It Cm example-config
Print an annotated configuration file, carrying every key at its default, to
standard output.
.El
.Sh PREFLIGHT
The agent runs nine checks before it starts and refuses to run if any of them
fails.
A warning does not stop it.
Each is printed as
.Ql <severity> <name>: <detail> ,
where the severity is
.Cm pass ,
.Cm warn
or
.Cm fail .
.Bl -tag -width "memory controller" -offset indent
.It Cm cgroup v2
The unified hierarchy is mounted.
Fatal.
.It Cm workload cgroup
The configured cgroup exists and the agent can read its counters and write its
limits.
Fatal, and it names every file it could not use.
.It Cm agent cgroup
The agent is not itself inside the cgroup it brakes.
Fatal when it provably is; a warning when the agent cannot tell, which is what
a cgroup namespace looks like from inside.
.It Cm memory controller
The memory controller is delegated to the cgroup's parent.
Fatal.
.It Cm auto-onlining
The kernel brings a hot-plugged block online by itself.
Fatal.
Under
.Cm offline
it adds the block and leaves it there, so the guest's
.Va MemTotal
never rises and no grant ever arrives.
Write
.Cm online
to
.Pa auto_online_blocks
under
.Pa /sys/devices/system/memory ,
or boot with
.Va memhp_default_state=online .
.It Cm transparent hugepages
The guest is not on
.Va transparent_hugepage=always .
Fatal by default; see
.Cm runtime.thp_always_fatal
in
.Xr pazari-agent.toml 5 .
.It Cm block size
.Pa /sys/devices/system/memory/block_size_bytes
can be read and is not zero.
Fatal.
This is the unit every grow is rounded to.
.It Cm balloon
No device on the virtio bus is a virtio-balloon.
Fatal when one is; a warning when a device will not say what it is.
A balloon moves the memory the guest has out from under the negotiation, so a
guest may have one or an agent, not both.
A guest on no virtio bus passes.
.It Cm swap
The guest has swap, and the workload cgroup may use it.
Never fatal, and skipped entirely when
.Cm engine.reclaim_swappiness
is zero.
A guest without swap cannot reclaim anonymous memory at all, so the brake is
the only thing between the workload and the kernel's out-of-memory killer.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev RUST_LOG
The log filter for standard error.
The default is
.Cm info .
.It Ev NOTIFY_SOCKET
Where the agent tells systemd it is ready, and where it sends watchdog pings.
Set by systemd under
.Va Type=notify ;
ignored when it is not set.
.It Ev WATCHDOG_USEC
The watchdog period systemd expects to be pinged within.
The agent pings at half of it.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/pazari/agent.toml
The default configuration file.
See
.Xr pazari-agent.toml 5 .
.It Pa /proc/meminfo
Read every tick for
.Va MemTotal ,
which is what the agent means by how much memory the guest has, and
.Va MemAvailable .
.It Pa /sys/devices/system/memory/block_size_bytes
Read once, for the unit every grow is rounded to.
.It Pa <cgroup>/memory.high , <cgroup>/memory.max
Written to place the band.
Under the systemd backend these are set as unit properties instead.
.It Pa <cgroup>/memory.current , <cgroup>/memory.events , <cgroup>/memory.pressure
Read every tick.
.Pa memory.events
is also held open and polled, so a throttle wakes the agent rather than waiting
for the next tick.
.It Pa <cgroup>/memory.reclaim
Written to free memory before it is offered back to the host.
.It Pa <cgroup>/memory.oom.group
Written once at startup, to arm or disarm killing the cgroup as a unit.
.El
.Pp
The agent also opens an
.Dv AF_NETLINK
socket on the kernel's uevent group, filtered to memory hot-plug events, so
that it learns a resize has landed without polling for it.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Pp
.Cm preflight
exits 0 when every check passed or warned, and 1 when any of them failed.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Check a guest before deploying an agent to it:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
pazari-agent preflight --config /etc/pazari/agent.toml
.Ed
.Pp
Write a configuration file to start from:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
pazari-agent example-config > /etc/pazari/agent.toml
.Ed
.Pp
The unit the guest module writes, in outline:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[Service]
Type=notify
ExecStart=/usr/bin/pazari-agent --config /etc/pazari/agent.toml
ExecStopPost=/usr/bin/pazari-agent panic-open --config /etc/pazari/agent.toml
WatchdogSec=30s
Restart=always
Slice=system.slice
.Ed
.Pp
.Va Slice=system.slice
keeps the agent out of the cgroup it brakes.
An agent inside that cgroup throttles itself, and preflight refuses to start
one that is.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pazari-stress 1 ,
.Xr pazarid 1 ,
.Xr pazari-agent.toml 5 ,
.Xr pazarid.toml 5 ,
.Xr pazari 7
.Pp
.Xr cgroups 7 ,
.Xr systemd.resource-control 5
